        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis is seems reasonable. However, I personally [have it overridden](https://github.com/echasnovski/nvim/blob/535ed97e480b89cb7e7e33c95f9559ba5091a0e3/src/mappings.lua#L35-L38) to force mode change. And it was like this since introduction of 'mini.basics'. I am not entirely sure why it is like it is, but I am sure there was a reason (probably to have all toggle mappings in 'mini.basics' consistently not trigger mode change).\r\n\r\nI'll take a look into the best ways to resolve this: either update `\\h` mapping in 'mini.basics' or document how it can be updated to work better with 'mini.map'.",
